Alpine MTB Map - licences
=========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Vincent Emonet and contributors

This repository holds three different kinds of thing, and they cannot all carry
the same licence. Which one applies depends on the file:

    public/alpine-mtb-map.kml                ODbL 1.0        (section 1)
    public/alpine-mtb-map.gpx
    public/alpine-mtb-map.geojson

    src/, scripts/, index.html,              MIT             (section 2)
    vite.config.js, package.json, .github/

Map tiles are not part of this repository. They are served by, and remain the
property of, OpenStreetMap, OpenTopoMap (CC BY-SA) and CyclOSM.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. MAP DATA - Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Covers public/alpine-mtb-map.kml, public/alpine-mtb-map.gpx and
public/alpine-mtb-map.geojson.

These files contain information derived from OpenStreetMap. The trail
geometries (the <LineString> / LineString coordinates) were extracted from
OpenStreetMap relations, which makes this a derivative database under the Open
Database License. ODbL is share-alike, so the database as a whole is released
under the same terms.

    Data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Full licence text:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

You are free to:

  Share  - copy, distribute and use the database
  Create - produce works from the database
  Adapt  - modify, transform and build upon the database

As long as you:

  Attribute - in any public use of the database, or works produced from it,
    you must keep the notice above and make clear that the data is available
    under the ODbL.
  Share-Alike - if you publicly use any adapted version of this database, or
    works produced from an adapted database, you must also offer that adapted
    database under the ODbL.
  Keep open - if you redistribute the database, or an adapted version of it,
    you may use technological measures that restrict the work (such as DRM)
    only if you also redistribute a version without such measures.

Individual contents of the database - the descriptive text, prices, travel
times and trail notes - are additionally made available under the Database
Contents License (DbCL) v1.0, mirroring how OpenStreetMap separates its
database licence from its contents licence:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/


